    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0385" n="339" xml:id="pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/5813a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: The more I consider the
                    matter the more I am convinced that it would be unwise for Mr. Root or any of
                    the Diplomatic Mission with him to stop in Japan on their return to the United
                    States. We are informed that they are leaving Petrograd about the 9th of this
                    month. The present unrest in the Far East and the possible divergence of views
                    of Mr. Root as to the policy of this Administration in regard to that region
                    seems to me to make it unwise for him to represent the Government. If it is
                    advisable to send a mission to Japan I think we should pursue the course of
                    sending new men directly from the United States.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
